%S A401087 1,3,3,1,3,9,3,5,1,9,3,3,3,9,9,3,3,3,3,3,9,9,3,15,1,9,5,3,3,27,3,8,9,
%T A401087 9,9,1,3,9,9,15,3,27,3,3,3,9,3,9,1,3,9,3,3,15,9,15,9,9,3,9,3,9,3,6,9,
%U A401087 27,3,3,9,27,3,5,3,9,3,3,9,27,3,9,3,9,3,9,9,9,9,15
%N A401087 The number of ordered pairs of exponentially odd divisors (d_1, d_2) of n such that d_1 * d_2 is a multiple of n.
%H A401087 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A401087/b401087.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%F A401087 Multiplicative with a(p^e) = (e^2+4*e+19)/8 if e is odd, and e*(e+2)/8 if e is even.
%F A401087 Dirichlet g.f.: zeta(s)^3 * Product_{p prime} (1 + 2/p^s - 4/p^(2*s) + 3/p^(4*s) - 1/p^(5*s))/(1 + 1/p^s)^2.
%t A401087 f[p_, e_] := If[OddQ[e], (e^2+4*e+19)/8, e*(e+2)/8]; a[1] = 1; a[n_] := Times @@ f @@@ FactorInteger[n]; Array[a, 88]
%o A401087 (PARI) a(n) = vecprod(apply(e -> if(e % 2, (e^2+4*e+19)/8, e*(e+2)/8), factor(n)[, 2]));
%Y A401087 Cf. A268335, A365345, A401083, A401086.
%K A401087 nonn,mult,easy,new
%O A401087 1,2
%A A401087 _Amiram Eldar_, Oct 14 2026
